\title{processdiagram: Publication-quality PROCESS-style mediation diagrams}
\description{
\code{processdiagram} creates publication-quality path diagrams and manuscript-ready
figure notes for supported PROCESS-style mediation models. It provides three
complementary workflows:
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=process_for_diagram]{process_for_diagram()}} runs a user-supplied PROCESS function, preserves a
seed, validates the supported path structure, and uses PROCESS's values as
the authoritative figure values.
\item \code{\link[=import_process_save2]{import_process_save2()}} reconstructs a diagram-ready object from compatible
PROCESS \code{save = 2} output without rerunning the analysis.
\item \code{\link[=fit_process_diagram]{fit_process_diagram()}} fits supported models with an independent native
engine.
}

The current statistical scope includes PROCESS Models 4, 6, and 81, custom
lower-triangular b-matrix specifications, OLS mediator equations, and supported
dichotomous-Y models with a logistic final equation.
}
\section{Recommended workflow}{

For a new figure intended to report a PROCESS analysis, use
\code{\link[=process_for_diagram]{process_for_diagram()}}, inspect \verb{$validation}, then draw with \code{\link[=plot]{plot()}} and
export with \code{\link[=save_process_diagram]{save_process_diagram()}}. Use \code{\link[=figure_note]{figure_note()}} to generate the
corresponding manuscript figure note.
}

\section{Saved PROCESS analyses}{

Use \code{\link[=import_process_save2]{import_process_save2()}} when a PROCESS \code{save = 2}
result is available. The importer preserves the bootstrap values stored in that
file; it does not need the original bootstrap seed.
}

\section{Independence from PROCESS}{

PROCESS source code is not bundled with or redistributed by this package.
\code{process_for_diagram()} expects the user to make a compatible \code{process()}
function available in the R session.
}

